WEBVTT

00:17.330 --> 00:18.970
Hey, Levia...

00:18.970 --> 00:22.040
Aren't you a bit too relaxed?!

00:22.480 --> 00:24.950
Huh? You think so?

00:29.020 --> 00:31.420
All right, ready to go?

00:31.420 --> 00:33.300
Oh, very well.

00:33.300 --> 00:36.820
I'll tag along with you, no matter how far!

00:36.820 --> 00:39.810
You said that with such a 
cool look just yesterday!

00:39.810 --> 00:41.860
What's the problem?

00:41.860 --> 00:45.210
It's not like there's anything to do until 
we get to the Beastmen continent.

00:45.210 --> 00:47.060
Yeah, true, but still...

00:47.630 --> 00:51.190
Besides, I'm on boat duty 
after we get to the port.

00:51.510 --> 00:56.000
Seems like a small price to pay to 
employ a god of the seas for free.

00:56.000 --> 00:58.070
Well, I mean...

00:58.550 --> 01:01.580
The war stopped all ships,
so there's no other way.

01:02.280 --> 01:07.960
Can't you do some magic that lets us 
jump all the way there in one go?

01:08.290 --> 01:09.670
Transfer magic?

01:10.290 --> 01:12.410
Yeah, do that. You're a sea god, right?

01:12.410 --> 01:15.760
What do you think a god of the seas is?

01:15.760 --> 01:19.050
Transfer magic is a huge hassle.

01:19.790 --> 01:21.330
Years of preparation!

01:21.330 --> 01:22.760
Extreme magic power!

01:22.760 --> 01:25.090
It's not something you can just throw around.

01:27.600 --> 01:32.040
I guess nobody would use horse-drawn
 carriages or ships if it were that easy.

01:32.040 --> 01:36.450
Travel takes effort. So...

01:37.860 --> 01:42.240
It only makes sense to receive proper 
compensation for that, don't you think?

01:55.360 --> 01:56.550
We stopped.

01:58.640 --> 02:00.140
Thank you!

02:04.390 --> 02:05.760
Sorry!

02:05.760 --> 02:08.220
We'd like to share this ride with 
you until we get to town...

02:17.120 --> 02:18.360
Big Sis?

02:18.690 --> 02:20.690
What, you know her?

02:20.690 --> 02:23.370
Long time no see, Crybaby Alizee!

02:23.830 --> 02:26.360
Master Setsu...

02:26.360 --> 02:29.660
That was a long time ago!

02:29.660 --> 02:34.110
I'm not a crybaby anymore!

02:34.110 --> 02:36.350
I'm not going to cry!

04:14.270 --> 04:18.940
<b><i>Episode 6</i></b>

04:14.270 --> 04:18.940
<b><i>Master and Pupil for a Second Time</i></b>

04:20.330 --> 04:22.360
This is Alizee Ifreel.

04:22.640 --> 04:27.030
We traveled together for a while 
the last time I was summoned.

04:27.030 --> 04:29.420
I am Master Setsu's top pupil!

04:29.420 --> 04:31.290
I don't remember ever 
taking you on as a pupil.

04:31.290 --> 04:33.160
What are you talking about?!

04:33.160 --> 04:39.000
You taught me the fundamentals of combat 
every night, physically and painstakingly!

04:39.350 --> 04:41.080
Every night, physically, huh?

04:41.080 --> 04:45.570
Okay, I get that he's my sister's teacher.

04:45.570 --> 04:46.890
And who are you?

04:46.890 --> 04:49.850
Oh, this is Amelle.

04:49.850 --> 04:51.850
I'm Alizee's little sister!

04:52.290 --> 04:54.230
You have a sister?

04:54.700 --> 04:58.450
Well, more like... things kind 
of ended up that way.

04:58.450 --> 05:01.440
I'm her sister! We lived together!

05:01.440 --> 05:03.610
Only for a short while, though.

05:04.280 --> 05:06.610
Like master, like pupil, huh?

05:07.130 --> 05:12.230
Anyway, Master, where have you been for five 
whole years? Leaving your top pupil behind?!

05:12.230 --> 05:14.370
Well, about that—

05:15.280 --> 05:17.880
I-I'll explain.

05:24.380 --> 05:25.630
I see.

05:25.930 --> 05:30.640
And now you're trying to thwart Toma's plan.

05:31.420 --> 05:36.500
Traveling across worlds twice, 
changing your appearance...

05:36.500 --> 05:38.770
From anyone but you, I'd never believe it.

05:39.250 --> 05:41.150
Yeah, but it's Setsu.

05:41.510 --> 05:43.420
I wasn't expecting any of it, either.

05:44.010 --> 05:47.780
Hey, I know! Alizee, come with 
us to the Beastmen continent.

05:48.150 --> 05:51.620
Help me out on my trip, 
like you did five years ago.

05:54.580 --> 05:56.000
Certainly!

05:56.000 --> 05:58.170
...would once have been my response, but...

06:01.070 --> 06:06.100
I'm actually caught up in a 
serious situation, as well.

06:06.100 --> 06:09.550
I'm sorry. It's all because of me.

06:14.470 --> 06:16.530
Ever since you vanished,

06:16.530 --> 06:21.060
I started taking on jobs fighting monsters
 as a continuation of my training.

06:21.380 --> 06:26.950
One day, I accepted a village's 
request to slay a dragon.

06:32.380 --> 06:34.430
That village was called Zathrow.

06:34.430 --> 06:36.620
It was a nice, quiet village.

06:36.620 --> 06:40.170
Please use this house while you're with us.

06:46.090 --> 06:49.720
She's an important guest, 
so please take care of her.

06:49.720 --> 06:52.720
Hello, I'm Amelle. Nice to meet you.

06:52.960 --> 06:55.720
Nice to meet you, too.

06:59.990 --> 07:01.910
Do you like it?

07:01.910 --> 07:07.730
Yes. Back at Evilbarrow, it's hard 
to find food this fresh right now.

07:08.140 --> 07:12.240
Right, you're at war with the humans...

07:12.710 --> 07:15.300
Oh, I have fruits, too!

07:15.300 --> 07:17.700
You don't have to go to so much trouble.

07:18.420 --> 07:20.460
Do you live here all alone?

07:20.950 --> 07:23.080
No, this...

07:24.210 --> 07:25.840
used to be my brother's house.

07:26.200 --> 07:27.380
Your brother?

07:27.380 --> 07:30.090
I'm not from this village.

07:30.430 --> 07:33.560
My brother found me about two years ago.

07:33.560 --> 07:37.860
He said, "Starting today, we're a family."

07:39.270 --> 07:42.100
So I lived here with him, but...

07:42.770 --> 07:47.520
He hasn't come home since the 
day the dragon first appeared.

07:48.640 --> 07:51.250
So I'm alone again.

07:52.110 --> 07:58.620
But it's fine! I've been alone all 
of my life, so I'm used to it.

08:02.720 --> 08:06.110
Amelle, this is a nice village.

08:06.110 --> 08:09.130
The food is good, and the villagers are kind.

08:10.350 --> 08:13.150
I'm growing a bit tired of traveling,

08:13.150 --> 08:17.100
so once this issue is settled, 
I'd like to stay here for a while.

08:17.380 --> 08:21.850
Oh, please do! This house is 
too big for me to live in alone.

08:22.190 --> 08:26.100
So, during that time, 
you can treat me as a sister.

08:28.640 --> 08:32.110
Would you really be my big sister?

08:32.110 --> 08:35.430
Sure. I mean, if it's okay with you.

08:35.430 --> 08:37.320
Of course, Big Sis!

08:40.420 --> 08:42.120
Can I ask you something?

08:43.150 --> 08:48.570
Is Amelle's brother missing because 
he was killed by the dragon?

08:48.570 --> 08:49.590
Hey...

08:51.280 --> 08:54.340
Actually, it seems like that's not the case.

08:56.890 --> 08:59.610
Every time there's a dragon attack,

08:59.610 --> 09:05.100
several villagers go missing. 
It wasn't just her brother.

09:05.580 --> 09:07.100
Missing?

09:07.460 --> 09:12.440
Yes. Normally, if a dragon attacks, 
it leaves some evidence of a battle behind.

09:12.440 --> 09:14.900
Even if the people are defeated,

09:14.900 --> 09:17.000
they should leave something behind.

09:17.750 --> 09:24.580
But everyone disappears without
the slightest trace, no exceptions.

09:25.280 --> 09:28.320
Doesn't sound like a normal attack.

09:28.320 --> 09:30.130
Like they're being spirited away.

09:34.370 --> 09:37.830
I thought the first order of business 
would be to defeat the dragon,

09:37.830 --> 09:39.890
so I took a drastic measure.

09:40.790 --> 09:42.140
What are you doing?

09:43.240 --> 09:45.390
I was disabling the ward against evil.

09:45.670 --> 09:49.170
What?! Then the dragon can come right here!

09:49.170 --> 09:51.020
That's the plan.

09:51.020 --> 09:53.150
I'm going to lure it in and beat it here.

09:53.790 --> 09:56.530
But that would put you in danger...

09:56.530 --> 09:57.820
I'll be fine.

09:57.820 --> 10:01.060
It's going to get dangerous here soon,
so head back home, okay?

10:02.280 --> 10:03.400
Okay.

10:04.820 --> 10:05.950
What's wrong?

10:06.340 --> 10:09.960
Well... I wanted to show you this.

10:13.030 --> 10:14.210
How pretty...

10:14.210 --> 10:17.380
Isn't it? I'm good at catching these!

10:18.580 --> 10:22.720
Aw, and I caught that one for you, too...

10:23.280 --> 10:26.220
It kinda tickles when you call me that.

10:27.640 --> 10:31.240
I have to introduce you to Big Bro, too!

10:31.240 --> 10:34.460
Big Sis! Big Sis! Big Sis!

10:56.290 --> 11:03.470
I cornered the dragon and went 
after it to finish it off, but...

11:07.770 --> 11:10.980
I lost track of it, so I returned 
to the village, only to find...

11:14.470 --> 11:19.100
that the rest of the villagers 
had gone missing, as well.

11:24.800 --> 11:27.580
All except for her.

11:33.120 --> 11:39.000
At dawn, I decided to go to the city 
to have someone take care of her.

11:39.000 --> 11:42.990
And then you bumped into 
us and hitched a ride.

11:42.990 --> 11:43.750
Yes.

11:44.380 --> 11:46.840
If what you said is accurate, 
that's a big deal.

11:46.840 --> 11:49.090
An entire village gone missing?

11:49.810 --> 11:56.590
Yes. I want to find her brother and allow 
her to live peacefully in the village, but...

11:57.000 --> 11:58.610
I don't understand what's going on.

11:59.080 --> 12:01.700
Do you have any ideas, Master?

12:01.700 --> 12:04.640
Does a "kidnapping dragon" ring any bells?

12:04.640 --> 12:07.880
I've honestly never heard 
of anything like that,

12:07.880 --> 12:09.800
but I'm willing to help.

12:09.800 --> 12:12.210
We can't pretend we didn't hear anything.

12:12.450 --> 12:13.710
Really?!

12:14.000 --> 12:16.960
Yeah. My precious pupil 
is in trouble, after all.

12:16.960 --> 12:18.950
Master...

12:18.950 --> 12:21.950
Thank you, Master Setsu, and... um...

12:21.950 --> 12:23.220
Mrs. Setsu!

12:30.650 --> 12:33.590
This incident can be explained by...

12:33.590 --> 12:34.560
zombies.

12:34.860 --> 12:35.990
Zombies?

12:38.320 --> 12:42.320
The whole village became the walking dead!

12:42.680 --> 12:47.320
There's actually an evil necromancer 
among the villagers.

12:47.320 --> 12:51.600
I don't think there's anyone 
like that in my village...

12:51.600 --> 12:56.830
Besides, don't zombies increase 
in number, not disappear?

12:56.830 --> 12:58.630
Ah, the rare "Air Zombie."

12:59.260 --> 13:01.800
Once they become zombies, 
they become invisible.

13:04.300 --> 13:06.320
Never heard of that before.

13:06.320 --> 13:08.300
So what about the dragon, then?

13:08.560 --> 13:11.060
It was a dragon zombie, of course.

13:11.700 --> 13:14.000
There was a legend in a 
country somewhere out east,

13:14.000 --> 13:15.990
about a zombie that became a dragon...

13:18.200 --> 13:19.600
Take this seriously.

13:19.600 --> 13:22.820
Wait, what about a siren, then?

13:23.050 --> 13:28.240
Among sailors, when people go missing,
it's a given that sirens are behind it.

13:28.240 --> 13:33.330
They say a siren's song 
draws men into the ocean.

13:33.790 --> 13:36.480
I thought the village was in the mountains.

13:37.200 --> 13:39.000
Who knows?

13:39.000 --> 13:44.090
Maybe there's a siren who lives in the 
mountains because they love the food there.

13:44.090 --> 13:47.090
That's just... okay, maybe...

13:47.330 --> 13:51.610
Um, sea monsters have a distinct smell

13:51.610 --> 13:53.760
that makes them easy to identify,

13:53.760 --> 13:55.400
so I don't think that's it.

13:56.100 --> 14:00.230
Oh, Levia-san, you don't smell, of course.

14:01.160 --> 14:02.230
Huh? Do I stink?

14:02.230 --> 14:05.410
I've got it! The culprit is...

14:05.410 --> 14:06.740
Space aliens!

14:07.830 --> 14:09.240
Space aliens?

14:11.490 --> 14:14.100
Everyone knows about them in my world.

14:14.100 --> 14:17.470
They come from the moon aboard 
flying saucers and abduct humans.

14:17.470 --> 14:19.000
So they're the—

14:20.430 --> 14:22.420
Setsu, take this seriously.

14:23.090 --> 14:24.340
But, I mean...

14:25.350 --> 14:29.830
What if the dragon that attacked was 
an advanced species, like Levia?

14:29.830 --> 14:33.100
It could avoid pursuit by taking 
human form and hiding among villagers.

14:33.890 --> 14:38.520
Levia, you could make villagers 
vanish without a trace, right?

14:38.520 --> 14:43.110
Stop making me sound bad 
just because you're stumped.

14:43.110 --> 14:45.610
I can't and won't do that.

14:45.910 --> 14:49.610
Huh? Levia-san, are you a dragon?

14:49.950 --> 14:51.220
No.

14:51.220 --> 14:54.100
But you do look kind of like one,
 don't you think?

14:54.100 --> 14:55.500
Not at all!

14:55.500 --> 14:58.750
Stop comparing me, a god of the seas,
 to a mere dragon.

14:59.940 --> 15:01.500
G-God of the seas?

15:01.500 --> 15:04.060
Assuming such a dragon exists,

15:04.060 --> 15:08.250
why didn't it use that magic 
to make Alizee disappear?

15:09.240 --> 15:10.510
Excuse me.

15:11.840 --> 15:15.530
It doesn't look like we'll be able to 
cross until the water settles down.

15:17.920 --> 15:19.320
Yikes.

15:19.720 --> 15:22.140
What are you going to do 
once you reach the city?

15:23.230 --> 15:28.330
I'll go back to the village of Zathrow and 
try to find evidence of the lost villagers.

15:28.330 --> 15:30.530
And you were going to do that alone?

15:31.860 --> 15:34.080
Now I have Master.

15:34.080 --> 15:35.320
Big Sis...

15:36.340 --> 15:42.000
Why did the dragon keep attacking
the village over and over, anyway?

15:42.000 --> 15:47.440
Well, maybe it was just really 
hungry and saw the humans as prey.

15:48.110 --> 15:52.680
Or maybe it was drawn there by magic power.

15:53.420 --> 15:54.430
Magic power?

15:54.430 --> 15:57.440
The magic power people 
use can attract monsters.

15:57.440 --> 16:01.940
For example, if you tried to use 
powerful magic inside the village,

16:02.430 --> 16:06.020
some monsters could 
potentially be attracted to it.

16:07.210 --> 16:08.550
I see.

16:08.550 --> 16:12.320
One more thing. Why did 
the villagers disappear?

16:12.320 --> 16:16.040
Even if magic power was the cause of this, 
it doesn't explain that part...

16:16.040 --> 16:18.770
People don't just evaporate into thin air.

16:18.770 --> 16:21.330
They had to have gone somewhere.

16:22.920 --> 16:25.980
Magic powerful enough to attract a dragon...

16:26.690 --> 16:29.500
Doesn't transfer magic fit the description?

16:31.330 --> 16:34.990
You said people vanished after every attack.

16:34.990 --> 16:37.010
What if it was the opposite?

16:37.010 --> 16:41.250
What if the attacks happened 
<i>after</i> people vanished?

16:41.590 --> 16:42.980
Do you mean...

16:42.980 --> 16:44.670
There's only one explanation.

16:44.670 --> 16:48.240
They were taken somewhere
using transfer magic.

16:48.240 --> 16:51.780
Every time that happened, 
the dragon got lured in by the magic power.

16:52.150 --> 16:56.710
B-But, Master, all magic needs a user.

16:56.710 --> 16:59.350
Are you saying someone was hiding nearby?

16:59.350 --> 17:04.500
Why don't you ask the user themselves?

17:05.160 --> 17:06.830
Think about it.

17:06.830 --> 17:10.000
Transfer magic is no quick task.

17:10.560 --> 17:13.020
It takes years of preparation, right?

17:13.610 --> 17:18.510
But wasn't there a person 
who arrived two years ago?

17:20.970 --> 17:25.270
W-Wait... Are you saying you suspect me?

17:25.600 --> 17:28.360
Hold on a minute. That's absurd.

17:28.360 --> 17:31.410
Space aliens were a more 
convincing alternative.

17:31.410 --> 17:33.640
Y-Yes, Master!

17:33.640 --> 17:37.160
She's the victim here! 
You can't treat her as the bad guy.

17:37.390 --> 17:39.590
At this point, sure.

17:40.410 --> 17:42.620
But I have one more question.

17:43.400 --> 17:46.450
When Levia was telling us the siren story,

17:46.450 --> 17:50.000
do you remember what you said?

17:50.420 --> 17:52.500
N-No...

17:53.380 --> 17:55.130
Sea monsters...

17:55.730 --> 18:00.550
Um, sea monsters have a distinct smell 
that makes them easy to identify.

18:02.210 --> 18:05.500
But most demons have a 
sense of smell like that.

18:05.500 --> 18:07.680
Levia is out of the ordinary.

18:07.680 --> 18:11.770
Even in her human form,
 she doesn't let her magic power leak out.

18:11.770 --> 18:14.270
Of course. I'm a sea god.

18:14.270 --> 18:16.490
Not even Alizee could tell.

18:16.800 --> 18:19.990
So how did you know what Levia really was?

18:27.200 --> 18:29.940
Well, that's because...

18:31.200 --> 18:32.500
I know...

18:34.370 --> 18:37.010
a thing or two about monsters.

18:47.130 --> 18:48.140
What happened?!

18:56.660 --> 18:59.610
She really was a dragon 
disguised as a human!

19:17.210 --> 19:19.440
I am Master Setsu's top pupil!

19:19.440 --> 19:21.380
I don't remember ever 
taking you on as a pupil.

19:22.740 --> 19:24.460
Do something, top pupil!

19:27.680 --> 19:29.480
Let's go, Alizee!

19:30.550 --> 19:31.460
Right!

19:51.520 --> 19:52.290
Levia!

19:52.660 --> 19:53.920
Got it!

20:09.740 --> 20:10.850
Alizee!

20:10.850 --> 20:11.640
Right!

20:40.270 --> 20:41.640
It's like snow...

21:05.420 --> 21:07.470
Are you sure it was okay 
to leave her on her own?

21:07.470 --> 21:10.500
Hmm? Oh, you mean Alizee?

21:10.500 --> 21:11.330
Yeah.

21:12.190 --> 21:16.630
We defeated the dragon, 
so she can take it from there alone.

21:17.360 --> 21:18.300
Besides...

21:19.050 --> 21:20.340
Besides?

21:20.340 --> 21:22.990
If she's going to call herself my pupil,

21:22.990 --> 21:25.990
she should finish the jobs she takes on.

21:27.080 --> 21:30.100
Well, how master-like of you.

21:56.650 --> 21:57.680
Amelle...

21:59.720 --> 22:02.840
I should introduce you to them, Big Sis.

22:06.380 --> 22:10.140
To my brother, to the other villagers...

22:10.730 --> 22:12.050
And...

22:13.440 --> 22:15.840
Amelle?! How...

22:17.960 --> 22:20.950
Oh, did you think I was dead?

22:20.950 --> 22:24.400
You really do have a dull sense of smell.

22:25.370 --> 22:30.410
These pets of mine and I have 
totally different smells.

22:31.560 --> 22:33.410
Where are the villagers?

22:33.850 --> 22:36.380
They turned into dolls.

22:36.780 --> 22:39.420
They all had strong magic power.

22:40.240 --> 22:41.490
Dolls?

22:42.320 --> 22:44.420
Don't give me that look.

22:45.000 --> 22:49.930
They need magic soldiers for the war.

22:51.490 --> 22:53.930
Amelle, you're...

22:54.580 --> 22:59.060
There was never anyone named Amelle.

23:01.090 --> 23:02.940
Who are you, then?

23:10.710 --> 23:13.950
I am Melluar, the monster master.

23:21.250 --> 23:24.320
Toma-sama gave me that name.

23:26.960 --> 23:31.970
<b><i>Next Time</i></b>

23:26.960 --> 23:31.970
<b><i>Visiting the Beastmen Continent for a Second Time</i></b>

23:27.490 --> 23:30.840
Next time: "Visiting the Beastmen 
Continent for a Second Time."
